  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th and Sarah Tan as the lead. The project initially had a Phase One budget of $500,000, but the executive board later approved a total budget of $2 million covering research, development, and marketing. Key developments include a call for AI-driven data visualization ideas by July 20th, the expansion of the team with Mike Chen and Lisa Ray, and the approval of a $15,000 training budget. Significant progress was reported in Phase Two regarding predictive analytics, with a detailed report due on November 20th. Additional updates include a compliance plan budget increase to $55,000, exploration of a partnership with TechInnovate, and a request for stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November."
